1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,357
In 1933,

2
00:00:01,357 --> 00:00:03,331
it became illegal for most Americans

3
00:00:03,331 --> 00:00:04,606
to own gold.

4
00:00:04,748 --> 00:00:07,220
President Roosevelt ordered citizens to hand

5
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,451
in their gold coins,

6
00:00:08,451 --> 00:00:09,926
bars and certificates,

7
00:00:09,926 --> 00:00:12,039
at twenty dollars and sixty-seven cents

8
00:00:12,039 --> 00:00:13,058
an ounce.

9
00:00:13,269 --> 00:00:14,975
Anyone who refused faced up to

10
00:00:14,975 --> 00:00:16,506
ten years in prison.

11
00:00:16,647 --> 00:00:17,147
Then,

12
00:00:17,147 --> 00:00:18,075
months later,

13
00:00:18,075 --> 00:00:19,794
Washington raised the price of gold

14
00:00:19,794 --> 00:00:21,440
to thirty-five dollars.

15
00:00:21,837 --> 00:00:22,476
Overnight,

16
00:00:22,476 --> 00:00:23,718
the dollar in your pocket was

17
00:00:23,718 --> 00:00:25,413
worth about forty percent less in

18
00:00:25,413 --> 00:00:26,235
gold.

19
00:00:26,376 --> 00:00:28,072
The government didn't take your money.

20
00:00:28,072 --> 00:00:29,453
It changed what your money was

21
00:00:29,453 --> 00:00:30,496
worth.

